cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below, together with the original paper by Thuerey et al. (2020)."
title: "GroundFoil: deep learning for inverted airfoils in ground effect"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Muhammad Taimoor Aslam"
    family-names: "Sial"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2268-1977"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtsial/GroundFoil"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  GroundFoil predicts the RANS flow (pressure and velocity) around inverted airfoils in
  ground effect (F1 front wings) with a U-Net trained on our own simulations. It builds
  on a reproduction of the U-Net of Thuerey et al. (AIAA Journal, 2020) on OpenFOAM
  v2606, gmsh 4 and Docker. It contains the ground-effect data generator (OpenFOAM, Spalart-Allmaras model, moving
  ground, boundary-layer mesh), its verification and validation (high-resolution LES of
  a NACA 4412, wind-tunnel tests of the Tyrrell 026 wing, grid convergence), the
  smoothing of 1,462 UIUC airfoils, a parameter scan of where steady RANS converges in
  ground effect, the code that trains and tests the U-Net on the ground-effect data, and
  two smaller models for comparison: one that predicts only the downforce, and one that
  predicts the pressure and the friction along the wing's surface.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - RANS
  - OpenFOAM
  - deep learning
  - U-Net
  - surrogate model
  - airfoil
  - ground effect
  - Formula 1
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Deep Learning Methods for Reynolds-Averaged Navier-Stokes Simulations of Airfoil Flows"
    authors:
